  "note": "Re-judged 2026-11-06 by an independent auditor who authored none of the changes named. RFC 7911 Section 2: \"A BGP speaker that re-advertises a route MUST generate its own Path Identifier to be associated with the re-advertised route.\" 1e65b6d4bb changed two cited producers. adjOutWrite.allow gains a branch for sentForward.ownRouteWithdrawal, which only sendOwnRouteWithdrawal sets, for a stale-rail withdrawal with no sent receipt; the relayed withdrawals in the churn units do not set it, so they take the old path. writeUpdateBody now takes the receipt in a local and calls noteExportWrite, which can only raise the export watermark. Neither generates, rewrites or releases an identifier. All tagged units are byte-identical and were re-read, with the functional file's expectations and the interop checker. Colliding sources must leave under different identifiers on classic and MP rails, same-context, cross-context and unframed sources alike; replacement, attribute change and withdrawal must carry the identifier announced, read from recipient bytes; a sibling's withdrawal must not renumber a survivor; wrap must not hand a third source an occupied identifier; the checker compares FRR's identifiers across a real session reset. Inequality is asserted only between colliding paths, and the obligation is local assignment, not difference from the received number. Caveat on proof: the .ci positive tag reads identifier 0 against a received 1, which pins this build's assignment, and no test or record ran for this rejudgment. Verdict unchanged: enforced.",
